<title>USA: US productivity substantially under-measured -Rubin.</title>
<headline>US productivity substantially under-measured -Rubin.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. productivity is significantly higher than suggested by official economic statistics, Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;There is almost universal agreement ... that productivity is substantially under-measured,&quot; he told the House Budget Committee.</p>
</text>
